  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a new Virtual Fitting UI, aiming for a questionnaire approach to replace the free-form text input. Key steps include determining gender first. My plan is to make the questionnaire guided, step by step, for user ease.\n\n\n**Structuring the Data**\n\nI\'ve been working on structuring the data flow for the new Virtual Fitting UI. The questionnaire will collect gender (male, female, binary/other), body type, and style/occasion. The AI\'s role remains the same: sourcing clothes and generating recommendations from Google Search, including prices and direct buying links, but with the input derived from the structured data. I\'m focusing on modifying the frontend (`VirtualFitting.tsx`) to implement the multi-step form and passing structured data to the backend.\n\n\n**Implementing the Wizard**\n\nMy focus is now on implementing the multi-step wizard UI in `VirtualFitting.tsx`.  I\'m aiming for a luxury aesthetic, so it\'ll be a step-by-step form to collect gender, body build, and desired style/occasion, replacing the free text field. I\'m structuring data flow for the steps and corresponding state variables. Once the last choice is made, `handleGenerate` will trigger.\n\n\n\n**Defining the Steps**\n\nI\'ve defined the options for each questionnaire step: gender (Menswear, Womenswear, Gender Neutral), body types (Slim, Athletic, Broad, Curvy, Round), and styles (Casual, Formal, Streetwear, Minimalist, Avant-Garde). I\'m also architecting a UI state machine to guide the user: show gender options on step 1, body type on step 2, style on step 3, loader on step 4 while loading, and results when outfits are ready. The ability to go back between steps is also a key feature I\'m implementing.\n\n\n**Refining the Backend**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that the backend prompt already handles structured inputs well, such as \"Gender: Menswear, Body Type: Athletic / Muscular, Style: Luxury Streetwear\". I\'m making a minor update to the `server.ts` prompt to ensure it explicitly utilizes the provided profile data. Currently the update is: `The user has provided the following profile: ${preferences}...`.\n\n\n**Implementing State Variables**\n\nI\'m now incorporating state variables to manage the flow of the new UI wizard. I\'ve added state for the current step, user selections (gender, body type, style), loading status, outfits, and error messages. The `handleSelection` function manages the progression through the questionnaire, updating the selection state and advancing the step. If the user completes the final step, the `handleGenerate` function is triggered. This function sets the loading state, and constructs the preferences string, to pass to the backend.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
