    thinking: "**Designing the Wizard**\n\nOkay, I\'m shifting gears now. The `<motion.form>` component in `VirtualFitting.tsx` needs a complete overhaul, I\'m thinking of creating a wizard. Let\'s start sketching it out, I\'ve got the genders and body types in mind. Slim/Slender seems like a good start.\n\n\n**Constructing the Wizard Flow**\n\nI\'ve got the wizard flow pretty well defined, now. I\'m focusing on the component state management; I have defined steps (1 to 4) and selections that are made within each step, like gender and body type. I\'m thinking about how to handle the final selections and API calls at the end, eliminating unnecessary `preferences` state by constructing the string for the API call directly from the `selections` object.\n\n\n**Refining the State Management**\n\nI\'m now diving into the component\'s state. I\'m considering how to streamline state management. I\'ve got the basic structure for the wizard laid out. I\'m focusing on the component\'s internal state to reduce unnecessary re-renders. I\'m aiming for clarity in how selections update the UI, using the selection data to construct the API call directly. The API call is triggered right before execution.\n\n\n**Implementing the Wizard Logic**\n\nI\'m now implementing the core logic within the wizard. I\'ve defined `handleSelection` and `handleGenerate` functions that manage the state transitions between steps and generate the API call using the `selections` object. The preferences string will be built directly, reducing state overhead. I\'m also incorporating loading and error states for a better user experience, and I\'m ensuring the API call executes upon the final step.\n\n\n**Adding Navigation and Reset**\n\nOkay, I\'m integrating the back button and reset functionality now. I\'ve wired up the `handleBack` function to control step navigation, ensuring it goes back to the atrium when at step 1. I\'ve also implemented `resetWardrobe` to clear selections and start over. Now, I have added error handling, loading states, and reset functions in place.\n\n\n**Integrating the Outfits**\n\nNow, I\'m thinking about integrating an \"Start Over\" button, and I\'m ready to incorporate error handling, and loading states into the component. I\'m focusing on ensuring seamless step navigation and API execution, including resetting and back functionality.\n\n\n**Enhancing the UI**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual elements. The button\'s hover effect was problematic across themes. I\'ve re-written that section to determine dark mode or light mode and adjust the `hover` class accordingly. The buttons are more versatile. Now, the UI behaves nicely regardless of the theme.\n\n\n"
