  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Initial Parameters**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the initial parameters of this project. Specifically, I\'m analyzing the request, breaking down the user interface issues like the non-functioning top bar buttons. I am also investigating the icon addition for the menswear, womenswear, gender-neutral, and body type filters. The procurement of images is also in focus.\n\n\n**Defining Scope, Constraints**\n\nI\'ve scoped the project to only include clothing from Pakistani brands, including their prices. I\'m focusing on the technical feasibility next. Specifically, I\'m working to make the top bar buttons interactive; the request notes the entire UI is non-functional, with the top bar buttons not working. I\'ll connect \"Body Profiles\" or \"Collections\" to the fitting room. For other buttons, I\'m thinking of showing a \"Coming Soon\" message or simply switching views. I\'ll use `lucide-react` to implement the icons for the category and body type filters. The menswear icon can be `User` or `Shirt`, and the womenswear icon will be a `User`.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Choices**\n\nI\'m reconsidering the icon choices, specifically for the category and body type filters. The initial thought was to use gendered icons, but `lucide-react` lacks those. I\'m exploring abstract shapes, standard icons like `User`, or concept icons like `Shirt`, `ShoppingBag`, or `Gem`. I am now focusing on finding appropriate `lucide-react` icons such as `CircleUser`, `User`, `Users` , `UserRound` and similar. Alternatively, for categories, maybe `Palette`, `Gem`, or `Crown`, or maybe `Activity` or `Dumbbell` for body types are better. Additionally, I am looking at Gemini image generation to bypass unreliable search grounding of images.\n\n\n**Addressing Image Procurement**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag with the image requirement. While the user wants actual images from Pakistani brands, retrieving them directly from websites using Gemini is proving difficult. I\'m exploring options: generating photorealistic mockups via the image generation API, using placeholders, or trying to extract `og:image` tags. The initial goal of scraping image URLs from the web seems infeasible with the current tools. My next step is to inform the user of these limitations.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Image Solutions**\n\nI am now focusing on providing the best visual representation of outfits. I have an internal image-generation skill available that creates images from outfit descriptions. I\'ll utilize that. I\'ve re-written my prompt to include Pakistani brands like Khaadi, Sana Safinaz, and others in order to get real links, though. Also, I\'m thinking of creating a secondary, server-side endpoint that can use an image model.\n\n\n**Implementing Image Generation**\n\nI\'ve decided to implement an AI stylist feature! I\'ll add a new server-side endpoint, `/api/generate-image`, using `ai.models.generateImages` to return an image from the outfit description. This is fantastic! I also have a UI update in mind. I\'ll connect \"Body Profiles\" to trigger `onStartFitting`, and add click handlers to other top-bar buttons to show a \"Feature in development\" toast or give visual feedback. Finally, I will also update the wizard options by adding `lucide-react` icons. I\'m choosing icons such as `User`, `Star`, and `Users` for categories, and `Activity`, `Dumbbell`, etc. for body types.\n\n\n**Enhancing Image Accuracy**\n\nI\'m now refining the server-side image generation process. I\'ve updated the `gemini-3.6-flash` prompt to strongly focus on Pakistani clothing brands like Sapphire and Khaadi. I\'m adding a `/api/generate-outfit-image` endpoint to `server.ts`. This endpoint generates photorealistic images of the outfits from the outfit description, which is then displayed above the item list in `VirtualFitting.tsx`. This addresses the image retrieval problem by generating images with AI. I am also working on clearly communicating the solution to the user.\n\n\n**Verifying Image Retrieval**\n\nOkay, so I\'m double-checking the image retrieval using the image generation API. I\'m confirming that the `imageBytes` property is correctly accessed from the `@google/genai` library and from the image generation skill, to ensure the base64 image data is handled properly. I\'m focusing on the `generate-outfit-image` endpoint to confirm the base64 data extraction is working.\n\n\n"
