 the head circle `M18 20a6 6 0 0 0-12 0` path slightly. I will begin by adding the wavy hair SVG path. I will write some `tsx` code to verify the design.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Hair Curve**\n\nI am now focusing on the hair\'s curves. I have developed a path to create a long wavy hair silhouette by sketching out two Bezier curves for the wavy hair, connecting them for a flowing look. I have decided to use absolute coordinates for increased clarity. I will intersect the curve at the shoulder to provide a natural effect.\n\nI am finalizing the path and am prepared to integrate this. I will next update the `VirtualFitting.tsx` file and rebuild the applet.\n\n\n**Connecting the Hairline**\n\nI\'m now refining the hair\'s top section. Initially, I thought a bald spot might appear, but the starting points actually align with the head\'s circumference. To address this and achieve a more natural look, I\'m making the hair continuous by running it over the top of the head in a graceful arch. I am now evaluating the look of a continuous hairline.\n\n\n**Integrating the Final Icon**\n\nI\'m now satisfied with the hairline\'s continuous appearance, so I\'ve chosen to keep the full circle with overlapping hair, which aligns with the minimalist lucide aesthetic. I\'ve written the `tsx` code for `CategoryIconWoman`, which now looks clean and fits the 1px-stroke line-art style. Finally, I\'m ready to modify the `VirtualFitting.tsx` file and will inject `CategoryIconWoman` into the `CATEGORIES` array.\n\n\n"
