    thinking: "**Considering the Redesign**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the user\'s request. My initial goal is to replace the current \"womenswear\" icon, and I\'m analyzing the provided reference image. I\'m focusing on the solid black silhouette of a woman, especially her wavy hair, with the goal of creating a new SVG icon.\n\n\n**Tracing the Reference**\n\nI\'m now translating the reference image\'s essence into a clean SVG. It has a central face shape, wavy hair longer on one side, shoulders, and a neckline. The goal is a pixel-perfect outline to match the app\'s minimalist aesthetic, utilizing `stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"none\"` and adhering to the `lucide-react` styling principles.\n\n\n**Constructing the Icon Outline**\n\nI\'m now deep in the SVG path construction, seeking a close outline match to the reference image. I\'m focusing on creating that continuous outer hair shape and the inner face cutout. The plan is to start top-center, work the left side, then right side and finally connect to the shoulders. My challenge is to balance the image\'s curved hair, face, and shoulder lines using path commands. I\'m iterating on specific coordinates to achieve the desired silhouette for a visually appealing icon that feels cohesive and complete.\n\n\n**Refining the Silhouette**\n\nI\'ve been refining the SVG path commands, focusing on achieving the right balance for the face and hair outline. I\'m paying close attention to the shoulders, where the hair falls over them, and how the shoulder curves intersect with the hair. I\'m working with the coordinates. The hairline is tricky; I\'m adjusting it to capture the widow\'s peak and ensuring a smooth transition. I\'ve switched the path from `M` to `L`, so I am trying to fix that and keep the curves smooth.\n\n\n**Finalizing the SVG Structure**\n\nI\'m now integrating the face and hair components, aiming for a unified silhouette. I have adjusted the face and hairline paths for a good balance. I am now incorporating the shoulder lines for the final outline. I\'m exploring the nuances of smooth hair and face transitions, with a focus on crafting a cohesive icon. I\'ve considered that the original reference is a solid black fill, but as a 1px stroke (to match lucide).\n\n\n**Analyzing the Hair Outline**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the hair\'s external outline, carefully considering its curvature and how it interacts with the face shape, and I\'ve started by defining the main parts of the head. I\'m visualizing the hairline\'s starting point and overall swoop to create the iconic silhouette. I am planning on keeping the face and hair disconnected to create a stroke-style image.\n\n\n**Refining the Symmetry**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the reference for balance. I noticed the widow\'s peak leans slightly left, but I\'m opting for symmetry to keep a clean, minimalist design. I am thinking of a parted-left hairstyle; however, I\'m considering exact replication to meet the initial instruction. I have determined the key coordinates to outline the face, hair and shoulders, and I\'m updating my SVG path accordingly.\n\n\n\n**Defining the Shoulders**\n\nI\'m now integrating shoulder lines, exploring vertical extensions from the chin, then shoulder curves. I\'m focusing on clean shoulder sweeps with `Q` commands, balancing the overall silhouette. I\'m incorporating the head and hair stroke with a deliberate face path, fine-tuning path commands and coordinates for a 1px stroke rendering that matches the reference. I\'m still adjusting the face and hairline paths.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Hair Curves**\n\nI\'m now iterating on the hair curves, focusing on smoothness. I\'m moving away from quadratic bezier (Q) commands, and testing cubic bezier (C) to avoid any unwanted sharpness. I\'m focusing on the left and right hair outlines and ensuring the flowing quality of the curves aligns with the reference image. The shoulder lines are coming together. I have finalized a full component, and the final design is almost done.\n\n\n**Adjusting the Connections**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the final SVG output, fixing connection issues and optimizing curves. I have replaced `M4.5` to `M4` with a cleaner connection. I\'m focusing on the flowing nature of the shoulders and ensuring they connect nicely. The final rendering now appears good.\n\n\n**Matching the Hair Waves**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the hair\'s detailed waves, ensuring they precisely mirror the reference\'s distinct bulges and curves. I\'m focusing on the left hair and right hair. To match the reference, I\'m thinking of filling it with `currentColor`, as the reference is solid. However, to match existing icons, I\'ll stick to stroke.\n\n\n**Refining the Hair\'s Appearance**\n\nI\'ve been further tuning the SVG path commands, now ensuring the hair flows naturally. I am focusing on the curves and waves. I\'m prioritizing accuracy for the hair\'s curves, now ensuring the icon precisely matches the feminine silhouette while adhering to the `lucide-react` style, to keep it clean. I have the neck in place, and the final icon is nearly done.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Silhouette**\n\nI am now focusing on the final details. I\'ve integrated the neckline, left and right shoulders. I refined the face, left hair, and right hair curves. The face shape, from widow\'s peak to chin, is now perfect. I am also working on smoothing the hair flow and connecting it. The final touches are in place, the icon is complete.\n\n\n**Implementing the Refinement**\n\nNow I\'m making final tweaks to integrate the precise shoulder adjustments, optimizing the hair curves, and cleaning up the connections. I\'ve switched the intersection points from `4.5` to `3.5` and `19.5` to `20.5`. I\'m verifying the smoothness of the curves, and the path for both left and right sides. I\'ve also verified a mental trace of the SVG to ensure no artifacts. I am confident that it now precisely matches the reference image, while still sticking to a 1px stroke