    thinking: "**Identifying the Bubble\'s Location**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the \"bubble\" as the `Sphere` component, rendered with a `MeshDistortMaterial`, residing within `ModelView.tsx`. Now, I need to figure out where to make the replacement for the bubble. I\'ll need to remember to remove the \"select theme\" buttons from `LuxuryUI.tsx`. My current focus will be on replacing the bubble with a real object, potentially in `ModelView.tsx` or `LuxuryUI.tsx`.\n\n\n**Replacing the Bubble\'s Purpose**\n\nI\'m now thinking about replacing the bubble with a masonry grid or carousel of actual images on the landing page. It seems the goal is to showcase real clothes, not a 3D bubble. The API integration will be postponed, and I\'ll work with a hardcoded array of clothing items for filtering. The home page, where the 3D bubble currently resides, might be transformed into a scrolling gallery of clothes.\n\n\n**Refining the Replacement Strategy**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the implementation plan. I will be removing the theme selector from `LuxuryUI.tsx`. Simultaneously, `ModelView.tsx` will undergo a transformation, replacing the bubble with a visually appealing grid or slideshow showcasing Pakistani brand clothing. Then, the API integration in `VirtualFitting.tsx` needs to be addressed. It\'s time to replace the API calls with a hardcoded mock database of Pakistani clothing items that can be filtered based on specific criteria. I\'ll need to define categories, body types, and styles to begin generating placeholder image data from Unsplash for brands.\n\n\n**Constructing the Data Source**\n\nI\'m now focused on the data. Since I can\'t scrape, I\'m building a realistic mock list of clothing items with the buy links and images. I\'ll utilize Unsplash images that evoke South Asian and Pakistani fashion styles to maintain authenticity, and I\'m creating a file `src/data/clothes.ts` to hold a mock database. The data will consist of an interface, `ClothingItem`, and an array called `CLOTHING_DATABASE`.\n\n\n**Populating the Mock Data**\n\nI\'m currently populating the `CLOTHING_DATABASE` with more items, each meticulously crafted to align with Pakistani fashion aesthetics, including links, images and descriptions. I\'m focusing on diverse categories, body types, and styles. I am ensuring price estimates are included, and links are present. I have 3 items currently, but will be adding more.\n\n\n**Expanding the Data Source**\n\nI\'m now expanding the mock data in `CLOTHING_DATABASE`. I\'ve added a few more items, paying close attention to diverse body types, styles, and categories to create a comprehensive representation. I will also make sure the images and descriptions are aligned to maintain a high degree of authenticity.\n\n\n**Designing the Gallery Component**\n\nI\'m now designing the `BrandGallery.tsx` component. This will replace `ModelView.tsx` to display clothing. I\'ll create a scrolling, animated grid for high-quality fashion images of clothes from the mock database, effectively transforming the landing page into a visual showcase. I also need to adjust `App.tsx` and ensure that I replace `ModelView` with `BrandGallery`. I will also check to see if the theme prop is needed. The background might just be an array of images. I think noir (dark) should be the default. I need to make sure to update the `src/data` folder too.\n\n\n**Refining the Outfits**\n\nI\'m now integrating the data and component changes. I am focusing on generating \"outfits\" within `VirtualFitting.tsx` by filtering the mock database, `CLOTHING_DATABASE`. I will be returning \"outfits\" containing the matched items. I am making sure the categories, styles and body types are being incorporated.\n\n\n"
