  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Developing Image Solutions**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `loremflickr.com` is dependable for image retrieval. Now, I\'m composing a Node.js script. The goal is to update the URLs in `clothes.ts` dynamically, using the item\'s name or category as the search term. Also, the background gallery, `BrandGallery.tsx`, should be enlarged to contain a greater number of images for display to the user.\n\n\n**Refining Image Sources**\n\nI\'m now focusing on restoring the original Unsplash URLs that weren\'t broken. I\'ve located the original `clothes.ts` content and can selectively re-paste the valid URLs to preserve those images. I\'m also considering `picsum.photos` for a background image array and have adjusted the URL structure to generate unique images, though their relevance to \"fashion\" is less certain. I\'m considering the possibility of a dedicated image array within `BrandGallery.tsx` and have re-evaluated using a seed from picsum for uniqueness.\n\n\n**Tracking Image Identifiers**\n\nI\'m now cataloging the original image identifiers from the conversations, focusing on the mapping of category codes to their corresponding image IDs. I\'m reconstructing the history, ensuring that I preserve the original mappings between the descriptive codes and the original IDs from the outputs. This also prepares for future migration strategies.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 15
      nanos: 317033077
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
