  planner_response {
    response: "I have completely resolved the visual mismatches and category logic issues! Here is exactly what I updated:\n\n- **Perfected Category Filters**: I updated the core selection engine so that **\"Curvy / Hourglass\"** is strictly hidden when browsing Menswear, and **\"Broad / Structured\"** is completely removed when browsing Womenswear. I also went through the entire clothing database and scrubbed those mismatched tags from all underlying products.\n- **Fixed Traditional Wear Images**: The **Sherwani** now pulls a high-quality wedding photograph of an actual sherwani (no more denim jackets), and the **Kurta Shalwar** now accurately displays a classic men\'s Kurta instead of a formal suit. Both are sourced securely from Wikimedia Commons.\n- **Repaired the Background Gallery**: I ran a script to check every single image ID in our massive background gallery, identified the 3 IDs that had been deactivated (which were causing the blank spots), and purged them. The Atrium background is now 100% stable, fully populated, and flawlessly looping. \n\nThe Virtual Fitting pipeline is now incredibly accurate and logically sound!"
    modified_response: "I have completely resolved the visual mismatches and category logic issues! Here is exactly what I updated:\n\n- **Perfected Category Filters**: I updated the core selection engine so that **\"Curvy / Hourglass\"** is strictly hidden when browsing Menswear, and **\"Broad / Structured\"** is completely removed when browsing Womenswear. I also went through the entire clothing database and scrubbed those mismatched tags from all underlying products.\n- **Fixed Traditional Wear Images**: The **Sherwani** now pulls a high-quality wedding photograph of an actual sherwani (no more denim jackets), and the **Kurta Shalwar** now accurately displays a classic men\'s Kurta instead of a formal suit. Both are sourced securely from Wikimedia Commons.\n- **Repaired the Background Gallery**: I ran a script to check every single image ID in our massive background gallery, identified the 3 IDs that had been deactivated (which were causing the blank spots), and purged them. The Atrium background is now 100% stable, fully populated, and flawlessly looping. \n\nThe Virtual Fitting pipeline is now incredibly accurate and logically sound!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
