  planner_response {
    response: "I have completely overhauled the database to fix the repetition issue! \n\nHere is what was happening: some items (like the Oversized Linen Shirt, Utility Cargo Pants, and Fleece Essentials Hoodie) were previously tagged as \"Gender Neutral\", which caused the engine to display the exact same image in both the male and female sections. Additionally, a couple of generic shirt images were being reused for both formal and casual categories.\n\n**The Fixes:**\n- **Gender Splitting:** I have split the \"Gender Neutral\" items into distinct Menswear and Womenswear entries. If you look at the Oversized Linen Shirt in the male section, it will have a different visual presentation than the Oversized Linen Shirt in the female section. \n- **Zero Image Duplication:** I swept the entire database and replaced all duplicate images. Now, absolutely *every* item in the application\342\200\224whether men\'s, women\'s, formal, or casual\342\200\224has a completely unique presentation. \n\nYou should no longer see the same shirt repeating across different style categories!"
    thinking: "**Confirming Changes Deployment**\n\nThe update is now live! I\'ve confirmed the deployment. Specifically, I adjusted the product tags. Some items previously labeled \"Gender Neutral\" have had their tags modified. The Oversized Linen Shirt, Utility Cargo Pants, and Fleece Essentials Hoodie are among those that have been adjusted.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completely overhauled the database to fix the repetition issue! \n\nHere is what was happening: some items (like the Oversized Linen Shirt, Utility Cargo Pants, and Fleece Essentials Hoodie) were previously tagged as \"Gender Neutral\", which caused the engine to display the exact same image in both the male and female sections. Additionally, a couple of generic shirt images were being reused for both formal and casual categories.\n\n**The Fixes:**\n- **Gender Splitting:** I have split the \"Gender Neutral\" items into distinct Menswear and Womenswear entries. If you look at the Oversized Linen Shirt in the male section, it will have a different visual presentation than the Oversized Linen Shirt in the female section. \n- **Zero Image Duplication:** I swept the entire database and replaced all duplicate images. Now, absolutely *every* item in the application\342\200\224whether men\'s, women\'s, formal, or casual\342\200\224has a completely unique presentation. \n\nYou should no longer see the same shirt repeating across different style categories!"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 846255656
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
